WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.350
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. Welcome back calculus
students. Today we're going to be

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.880
taking derivatives using the quotient rule. Let's
get right into it. On to our quotient

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:13.980
rule example. Here we have h of
x equals 2x plus 1

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:18.220
and x squared minus 3. Again, for
the quotient rule now,

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:23.480
we have still that f prime of g and our fg

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:27.080
prime, but this time it's a minus instead of
the positive that was in our product

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:31.900
rule, and we're dividing it over g squared for
our quotient rule. So first, I'd like

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:35.780
to start by identifying our f and g. Again, for
the product and quotient rule, it's

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.800
usually pretty easy to identify
those two functions.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:44.420
And I want to take, this is obviously
our f here, our f of x, and

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.300
this is our g of x.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:50.760
And just like how we did it for product rule, I
want to start by taking just these

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:56.220
two primes and then plugging them into our
quotient formula. So f prime of

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:01.440
x here will be the power rule of 2x,
which will just be 2 because

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.920
x will go to 1. And 1 is a constant, and all
constants always go to 0. So this

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:10.700
is our f of x prime. For our g prime of x,

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:17.360
it will be x squared power
rule, which is 2x,

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:22.460
and then minus 3, which is a constant. so that
will also go to zero. Now we have our

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:26.680
f prime of x and our g prime of x. Let's
plug them into our quotient rule.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:33.510
Our quotient rule will state
that h prime of x is

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.210
equal to f prime of x times g of
x. So this will be

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:43.250
2x squared minus 3, 2 times x squared
minus 3. And then you'll

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:48.410
subtract our f which is 2x plus 1

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:53.750
times our g prime which is 2x and
this is all divided by g of

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:59.210
x not g prime of x and that will be x
squared minus 3 all squared

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:04.610
now here we will expand the top a little
bit and we will get 2x squared

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:07.010
minus 6 minus

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:13.290
4x squared plus 2x this

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:19.860
is all over x squared minus 3 squared
and then we will apply the

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:25.320
negative in, it'll be 2x minus 6 minus 4x
squared minus 2 all over

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:30.340
x squared minus 3 all squared here we
have the like terms this

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:35.400
positive 2x squared and this
negative 4x squared

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:40.890
so we will be left with
negative 2x squared minus

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:45.090
2x minus 6 all over

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:50.920
x squared minus 3 squared if you want you
can factor out here a negative

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:55.940
2 but it is not required here If we factor out
negative 2, it will be x squared

00:02:55.790 --> 00:03:01.440
plus x plus 3 all over x

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:06.900
squared minus 3 all squared. And that is
our quotient rule. Easy peasy,

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:08.860
lemon squeezy. See you in the next one.
